# Handoff checklist

Cadence: [wrap-on-command.mdc](wrap-on-command.mdc). **CMPH** does not run this swarm.
**SWAT** / epic close does.

## When to write a note

- **CMPH:** scope shipped to `main`. Short Receiver brief. No Gates section.
- **SWAT / epic close:** last in-scope story (or they typed **SWAT**). Full gates below, then [epic-close.mdc](epic-close.mdc).
- **Mid-flight:** label WIP / blocked / needs decision. Do not write “ship complete.”

**Git truth:** story, version, `origin/main @ sha` or waiting-on-merge, **Do not**, **Next**.
Receivers trust it — [context-bootstrapper](../skills/context-bootstrapper/SKILL.md).

**CMPH git:** commit, merge `main`, push `origin main` ([no-auto-merge-main.mdc](no-auto-merge-main.mdc)).
Feature-branch-only push is not the default close-out.

## SWAT / epic close only (do not run on mid-epic CMPH)

1. **Code review** — code-reviewer skill. PASS/WARN/FAIL in the note under **Code review**.
2. **Dead code** — dead-code-remover on the epic’s new surface.
3. **Tech debt** — tech-debt-evaluator; promote persistent items into `TECH_DEBT.md`.
4. **Tests / coverage** — merge-ready command (include markdownlint). Note under **Tests**.
5. **Project readiness** — optional / N/A.
6. **Security** — only if the epic touched credentials, logging, remote access, networking, or files.
7. **Tier 2** — already done per story; quote last hitch vs prior. Do not re-smoke the epic unless a gate is missing.

Then status docs + GitHub Release per [epic-close.mdc](epic-close.mdc).

**Receiver brief in chat** — [`.cursor/handoff/_template.md`](../handoff/_template.md).
**Filename:** `docs/handoff/NNNN-HANDOFF-YYYY-MM-DD_HHmm.md` (never reuse `NNNN`).
Gates PASS/WARN belong in the **SWAT file only**, not in a mid-epic CMPH chat.
